IMPORT prelude

-- Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) -- the general protections, for an employee who has been dismissed, and the rules that let
-- only one dismissal claim run at a time.
--
-- SEAT: the employee. "Was my dismissal unlawful adverse action? Where can I take it, by when, what do I risk in costs,
-- and which other claims does taking it shut?" Every question below is phrased as that person would ask it, on facts
-- that person could state; every judgment the text hands to the FWC or a court is an input beginning "if ...".
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Workplace rights (s 341(1)); adverse action by an employer against an employee (s 342(1) item 1);
-- the workplace rights protection (s 340(1)); discrimination (s 351, with the anti-discrimination laws of s 351(3));
-- temporary absence for illness or injury (s 352, with reg 3.01); multiple reasons (s 360); the presumed reason
-- (s 361); the dismissal dispute: applying to the FWC (s 365), in time (s 366), the certificate (s 368(3)), arbitration
-- (s 369(1)), going to court (s 370); costs in a court (s 570) and before the FWC (s 611); unlawful termination is not
-- open to someone who can make a general protections court application (s 723); one dismissal claim at a time
-- (ss 725-733).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 73, compilation date 7 July 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 62, 2026; register id
-- C2026C00355), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2009A00028.txt.
-- Regulations used: Fair Work Regulations 2009 (F2009L02356), Compilation No. 57, compilation date 1 October 2026
-- (register id F2026C00996), reg 3.01 (prescribed illness or injury), as deposited at
-- ../../../fair-work-regulations-2009/registers/source-bundle/F2009L02356.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The other general protections (industrial activity, coercion, misrepresentation, sham contracting:
-- ss 343-350, 353-359), the protections for prospective employees, contractors and platform workers (s 342(1) items
-- 2-7); non-dismissal disputes (s 372); the remedies a court may order (s 545) and civil penalty amounts (s 539);
-- unlawful termination itself (Part 6-4) beyond s 723; costs against lawyers and agents (s 376) and the other FWC
-- costs powers (ss 400A, 401, 780); the Commonwealth's and States' costs (ss 569, 569A); the meaning of "workplace law"
-- and "workplace instrument" (asked as facts); whether an action is unlawful under an anti-discrimination law (asked
-- as a fact: the State and Commonwealth Acts are other subjects); the FWC and the courts as institutions.
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `Fair Work Act 2009 -- the general protections, for a dismissed employee`

§§ `ss 340-342, 351, 352, 360, 361 -- was my dismissal unlawful adverse action`

-- s 342(1), table item 1: adverse action is taken by "an employer against an employee" if "the employer: (a) dismisses
-- the employee; or (b) injures the employee in his or her employment; or (c) alters the position of the employee to
-- the employee's prejudice; or (d) discriminates between the employee and other employees of the employer."
@export Has my employer taken adverse action against me (s 342(1), item 1)?
GIVEN `my employer dismissed me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer dismissed you
      `my employer injured me in my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer injured you in your employment (for example, by cutting your pay or hours)
      `my employer changed my position to my prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer changed your position at work to your disadvantage
      `my employer treated me differently from other employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer discriminated between you and its other employees
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer taken adverse action against me` IF
        `my employer dismissed me`
    OR  `my employer injured me in my employment`
    OR  `my employer changed my position to my prejudice`
    OR  `my employer treated me differently from other employees`

-- s 341(1): "A person has a workplace right if the person: (a) is entitled to the benefit of, or has a role or
-- responsibility under, a workplace law, workplace instrument or order made by an industrial body; or (b) is able to
-- initiate, or participate in, a process or proceedings under a workplace law or workplace instrument; or (c) is able
-- to make a complaint or inquiry: (i) to a person or body having the capacity under a workplace law to seek compliance
-- with that law or a workplace instrument; or (ii) if the person is an employee -- in relation to his or her
-- employment." "Workplace law" and "workplace instrument" are defined in s 12 and asked here as facts.
@export Do I have a workplace right (s 341(1))?
GIVEN `I am entitled to a benefit under a workplace law, instrument or order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to a benefit (or have a role or responsibility) under a workplace law such as this Act, an award, an enterprise agreement or an order of an industrial body
      `I can start or take part in a process under a workplace law or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can start or take part in a process or proceeding under a workplace law or instrument (for example, a flexible working request or a dispute procedure)
      `I can complain to a body that enforces a workplace law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can make a complaint or inquiry to a body that can seek compliance with a workplace law (for example, the Fair Work Ombudsman)
      `I can complain or inquire about my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as an employee, you can make a complaint or inquiry about your employment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a workplace right` IF
        `I am entitled to a benefit under a workplace law, instrument or order`
    OR  `I can start or take part in a process under a workplace law or instrument`
    OR  `I can complain to a body that enforces a workplace law`
    OR  `I can complain or inquire about my employment`

-- s 360: "a person takes action for a particular reason if the reasons for the action include that reason."
-- s 361(1): where it is alleged "that a person took ... action for a particular reason" and taking it for that reason
-- "would constitute a contravention of this Part", "it is presumed that the action was ... taken for that reason ...
-- unless the person proves otherwise." (2) Not for an interim injunction.
@export Must my employer prove that it did not act for the reason I allege (s 361)?
GIVEN `I allege my employer acted for a reason this Part prohibits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application alleges that your employer acted for a reason that would contravene the general protections
      `I am asking only for an interim injunction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order you are asking for is only an interim injunction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer prove it did not act for that reason` IF
        `I allege my employer acted for a reason this Part prohibits`
    AND (NOT `I am asking only for an interim injunction`)

-- Whether the reason I allege is taken as established: alleged, presumed under s 361, and not disproved. s 360 makes
-- it enough that the reason was among the employer's reasons, so the employer must prove it was not one of them.
@export Is the reason I allege taken to be one of my employer's reasons (ss 360, 361)?
GIVEN `I allege my employer acted for a reason this Part prohibits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application alleges that your employer acted for a reason that would contravene the general protections
      `I am asking only for an interim injunction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order you are asking for is only an interim injunction
      `if my employer proves that reason was not among its reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied, on your employer's evidence, that the reason you allege was not one of its reasons
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the reason I allege taken to be one of its reasons` IF
        `Must my employer prove it did not act for that reason` `I allege my employer acted for a reason this Part prohibits` `I am asking only for an interim injunction`
    AND (NOT `if my employer proves that reason was not among its reasons`)

-- s 340(1): "A person must not take adverse action against another person: (a) because the other person: (i) has a
-- workplace right; or (ii) has, or has not, exercised a workplace right; or (iii) proposes or proposes not to ...
-- exercise a workplace right; or (b) to prevent the exercise of a workplace right by the other person."
@export Did my employer breach the workplace rights protection (s 340(1))?
GIVEN `my employer took adverse action against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer took adverse action against you (s 342)
      `I have a workplace right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a workplace right (s 341)
      `if my workplace right, or using it, was among the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your having, using, not using or proposing to use the workplace right, or stopping you using it, was among your employer's reasons (presumed unless your employer proves otherwise: s 361)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did my employer breach the workplace rights protection` IF
        `my employer took adverse action against me`
    AND `I have a workplace right`
    AND `if my workplace right, or using it, was among the reasons`

-- s 351(1): "An employer must not take adverse action against a person who is an employee ... because of the
-- person's race, colour, sex, sexual orientation, breastfeeding, gender identity, intersex status, age, physical or
-- mental disability, marital status, family or carer's responsibilities, subjection to family and domestic violence,
-- pregnancy, religion, political opinion, national extraction or social origin." The list is closed: an attribute not
-- in it is not protected by s 351 (other sections, or other laws, may protect it).
DECLARE `Protected attribute` IS ONE OF
    `race`
    `colour`
    `sex`
    `sexual orientation`
    `breastfeeding`
    `gender identity`
    `intersex status`
    `age`
    `physical or mental disability`
    `marital status`
    `family or carer's responsibilities`
    `subjection to family and domestic violence`
    `pregnancy`
    `religion`
    `political opinion`
    `national extraction`
    `social origin`

-- s 351(2): "However, subsection (1) does not apply to action that is: (a) not unlawful under any anti-discrimination
-- law in force in the place where the action is taken; or (b) taken because of the inherent requirements of the
-- particular position concerned; or (c) if the action is taken against a staff member of an institution conducted in
-- accordance with the doctrines ... of a particular religion or creed -- taken: (i) in good faith; and (ii) to avoid
-- injury to the religious susceptibilities of adherents of that religion or creed." s 351(3) lists the
-- anti-discrimination laws: the four Commonwealth Acts and one Act of each State and Territory (for Victoria, the Equal
-- Opportunity Act 2010). Whether the action is unlawful under one of them is another Act's question, asked as a fact.
@export Did my employer breach the discrimination protection (s 351)?
GIVEN `my employer took adverse action against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer took adverse action against you (s 342)
      `if this attribute of mine was among the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attribute was among your employer's reasons (presumed unless your employer proves otherwise: s 361)
      `the action is unlawful under an anti-discrimination law where it was taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action is unlawful under a Commonwealth anti-discrimination Act or the anti-discrimination Act of the State or Territory where it was taken (s 351(3) lists them)
      `if it was taken because of the inherent requirements of my position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action was taken because of the inherent requirements of your particular position
      `if a religious institution took it in good faith to avoid injury to its adherents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work for an institution run under a religion's doctrines and it acted in good faith to avoid injury to the religious susceptibilities of its adherents
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did my employer breach the discrimination protection` IF
        `my employer took adverse action against me`
    AND `if this attribute of mine was among the reasons`
    AND `the action is unlawful under an anti-discrimination law where it was taken`
    AND (NOT `if it was taken because of the inherent requirements of my position`)
    AND (NOT `if a religious institution took it in good faith to avoid injury to its adherents`)

-- s 352: "An employer must not dismiss an employee because the employee is temporarily absent from work because of
-- illness or injury of a kind prescribed by the regulations." Reg 3.01(2)-(4): prescribed if the employee gives "a
-- medical certificate ... or a statutory declaration ... within: (a) 24 hours after the commencement of the absence;
-- or (b) such longer period as is reasonable"; or complies with a workplace instrument's terms to notify and
-- substantiate the absence; or gave evidence for paid personal/carer's leave for personal illness or injury. (5) Not
-- prescribed if "(a) ... (i) the employee's absence extends for more than 3 months; or (ii) the total absences ...
-- within a 12 month period, have been more than 3 months ... and (b) the employee is not on paid personal/carer's leave
-- ... for the duration of the absence." (6) Time on workers' compensation is not paid personal/carer's leave.
@export Was I protected from being dismissed for being away ill or injured (s 352, reg 3.01)?
GIVEN `I was temporarily absent because of illness or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were temporarily absent from work because of an illness or injury
      `I gave a medical certificate or statutory declaration in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave a medical certificate or statutory declaration within 24 hours of the absence starting, or within a longer period that was reasonable
      `I notified and substantiated the absence as my award or agreement requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your award or agreement requires you to notify and substantiate an absence, and you did
      `I gave evidence for paid personal leave for the illness or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave your employer the evidence needed for paid personal/carer's leave for your illness or injury
      `this absence has lasted more than 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this absence has lasted more than 3 months
      `my absences in 12 months total more than 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your absences within a 12-month period add up to more than 3 months
      `I have been on paid personal leave for the whole absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been on paid personal/carer's leave for illness or injury for the whole absence (not counting time on workers' compensation)
      `if my absence was among the reasons I was dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your absence was among your employer's reasons for dismissing you (presumed unless your employer proves otherwise: s 361)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I protected from dismissal for being away ill or injured` IF
        `I was temporarily absent because of illness or injury`
    AND `if my absence was among the reasons I was dismissed`
    AND (    `I gave a medical certificate or statutory declaration in time`
         OR  `I notified and substantiated the absence as my award or agreement requires`
         OR  `I gave evidence for paid personal leave for the illness or injury`)
    AND (NOT (    (`this absence has lasted more than 3 months` OR `my absences in 12 months total more than 3 months`)
              AND (NOT `I have been on paid personal leave for the whole absence`)))

§§ `ss 365, 366, 368, 369, 370 -- taking a dismissal to the FWC, and then to court (if I have been dismissed)`

-- s 365: if a person "alleges that the person was dismissed in contravention of this Part, the person ... may apply to
-- the FWC for the FWC to deal with the dispute." s 366(1): "within 21 days after the alleged dismissal took effect; or
-- (b) within such further period as the FWC allows" for "exceptional circumstances" (s 366(2)).
@export Am I still in time to apply to the FWC about a dismissal in breach of the general protections (ss 365, 366)?
GIVEN `days since the dismissal took effect` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since your dismissal took effect
      `if the FWC allows a further period for exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Fair Work Commission allows you more time because of exceptional circumstances
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time to apply to the FWC about the dismissal` IF
        `days since the dismissal took effect` AT MOST 21
    OR  `if the FWC allows a further period for exceptional circumstances`

-- s 370: someone entitled to apply under s 365 "must not make a general protections court application ... unless:
-- (a) both of the following apply: (i) the FWC has issued a certificate under paragraph 368(3)(a) ...; (ii) the
-- general protections court application is made within 14 days after the day the certificate is issued, or within
-- such period as the court allows ...; or (b) the general protections court application includes an application for
-- an interim injunction." s 368(3)(a): the FWC "must issue a certificate" if "satisfied that all reasonable attempts to
-- resolve the dispute (other than by arbitration) have been, or are likely to be, unsuccessful".
@export May I take my general protections dismissal claim to court (s 370)?
GIVEN `the FWC has issued a certificate that the dispute could not be resolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Fair Work Commission has issued a certificate that all reasonable attempts to resolve your dismissal dispute have failed (s 368(3)(a))
      `days since the certificate was issued` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the certificate was issued (0 if none has been)
      `if the court allows a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court allows you more than 14 days after the certificate
      `my application includes an interim injunction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your court application includes an application for an interim injunction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I take my dismissal claim to court` IF
        (    `the FWC has issued a certificate that the dispute could not be resolved`
         AND (`days since the certificate was issued` AT MOST 14 OR `if the court allows a longer period`))
    OR  `my application includes an interim injunction`

-- s 369(1): the FWC may arbitrate if "(a) the FWC issues a certificate under paragraph 368(3)(a) ...; and (b) the
-- parties notify the FWC that they agree to the FWC arbitrating the dispute; and (c) the notification: (i) is given
-- ... within 14 days after the day the certificate is issued, or within such period as the FWC allows ...; and (ii)
-- complies with any requirements prescribed by the procedural rules; and (d) sections 726, 728, 729, 730, 731 and 732
-- do not apply" (that is, no other dismissal claim of those kinds is on foot). Once notified, s 727(1A) shuts the
-- court (note 1 to s 370).
@export Can the FWC arbitrate my general protections dismissal dispute (s 369(1))?
GIVEN `the FWC has issued a certificate that the dispute could not be resolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Fair Work Commission has issued a certificate that all reasonable attempts to resolve your dismissal dispute have failed (s 368(3)(a))
      `my employer and I both agree to arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your employer both notify the Commission that you agree to it arbitrating the dispute
      `days since the certificate was issued` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the certificate to the notification
      `if the FWC allows a longer period to notify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission allows more than 14 days for the notification
      `the notification complies with the procedural rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notification meets the Commission's procedural rules
      `another dismissal claim of mine is on foot` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have another live claim or complaint about the dismissal (a bargaining order, unfair dismissal or unlawful termination application, a general protections court application, or a complaint under another law)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the FWC arbitrate my dismissal dispute` IF
        `the FWC has issued a certificate that the dispute could not be resolved`
    AND `my employer and I both agree to arbitration`
    AND (`days since the certificate was issued` AT MOST 14 OR `if the FWC allows a longer period to notify`)
    AND `the notification complies with the procedural rules`
    AND (NOT `another dismissal claim of mine is on foot`)

§§ `ss 570, 611 -- what I risk in costs`

-- s 611(1): "A person must bear the person's own costs in relation to a matter before the FWC." (2) The FWC "may
-- order" costs only "if: (a) the FWC is satisfied that the first person made the application ... vexatiously or without
-- reasonable cause; or (b) the FWC is satisfied that it should have been reasonably apparent to the first person that
-- the first person's application ... had no reasonable prospect of success." The note names further powers (ss 376,
-- 400A, 401, 780), not encoded.
@export Can the FWC order me to pay my employer's costs of my application (s 611)?
GIVEN `if the FWC is satisfied I applied vexatiously or without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Fair Work Commission is satisfied you made the application vexatiously or without reasonable cause
      `if the FWC is satisfied I should have seen it had no reasonable prospect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is satisfied it should have been reasonably apparent to you that your application had no reasonable prospect of success
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the FWC order me to pay costs` IF
        `if the FWC is satisfied I applied vexatiously or without reasonable cause`
    OR  `if the FWC is satisfied I should have seen it had no reasonable prospect`

-- s 570(1): in "proceedings ... in a court ... in relation to a matter arising under this Act", a party "may be
-- ordered ... to pay costs ... only in accordance with subsection (2)" (or ss 569, 569A, which concern the Commonwealth
-- and the States). (2): "only if: (a) the court is satisfied that the party instituted the proceedings vexatiously or
-- without reasonable cause; or (b) the court is satisfied that the party's unreasonable act or omission caused the
-- other party to incur the costs; or (c) the court is satisfied of both of the following: (i) the party unreasonably
-- refused to participate in a matter before the FWC; (ii) the matter arose from the same facts as the proceedings."
@export Can a court order me to pay my employer's costs of a Fair Work Act claim (s 570)?
GIVEN `if the court is satisfied I sued vexatiously or without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied you started the proceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause
      `if the court is satisfied my unreasonable act or omission caused the costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that something unreasonable you did, or failed to do, caused your employer the costs
      `if the court is satisfied I unreasonably refused to take part at the FWC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied you unreasonably refused to take part in a matter before the Fair Work Commission
      `the FWC matter arose from the same facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that Commission matter arose from the same facts as the court proceedings
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a court order me to pay costs of a Fair Work claim` IF
        `if the court is satisfied I sued vexatiously or without reasonable cause`
    OR  `if the court is satisfied my unreasonable act or omission caused the costs`
    OR  (    `if the court is satisfied I unreasonably refused to take part at the FWC`
         AND `the FWC matter arose from the same facts`)

§§ `ss 723, 725-733 -- one dismissal claim at a time (if I have been dismissed)`

-- s 725: "A person who has been dismissed, or allegedly dismissed, must not make an application or complaint of a kind
-- referred to in any one of sections 726 to 732 in relation to the dismissal, or alleged dismissal, if any other of
-- those sections applies." The seven kinds:
DECLARE `Dismissal claim` IS ONE OF
    `a bargaining order application (s 726)`
    `a general protections application to the FWC (s 727)`
    `a general protections court application (s 728)`
    `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)`
    `an unlawful termination application to the FWC (s 730)`
    `an unlawful termination court application (s 731)`
    `a complaint under another law (s 732)`

-- What happened to a claim already made. Each of ss 726-732 "applies" while the claim has not been withdrawn and has not
-- failed for want of jurisdiction; ss 727 and 730 also stop applying when the FWC issues its certificate, unless the
-- parties then notify it that they agree to arbitration (ss 727(1A), 730(1A)); s 729 also stops applying when the
-- application fails because the FWC found a genuine redundancy. s 733: a claim made only about a benefit owed because
-- of the dismissal is not one "in relation to a dismissal". s 732(3): a complaint under the Australian Human Rights
-- Commission Act 1986 that reaches the dismissal only by amendment counts from the amendment.
DECLARE `Earlier claim` HAS
    `its kind` IS A `Dismissal claim`
    `it is about the dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is only about benefits owed because of the dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I withdrew it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it failed for want of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the FWC issued its certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties then agreed to FWC arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it failed because the FWC found a genuine redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ss 726-732: whether the section for this earlier claim "applies".
@export Does this earlier claim still count against my other dismissal claims (ss 726-733)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Earlier claim` @desc A claim or complaint you have already made about the dismissal, and what has happened to it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this earlier claim still count` IF
        `the claim`'s `it is about the dismissal`
    AND (NOT `the claim`'s `it is only about benefits owed because of the dismissal`)
    AND (NOT `the claim`'s `I withdrew it`)
    AND (NOT `the claim`'s `it failed for want of jurisdiction`)
    AND `the kind-specific release has not happened`
    WHERE
        `the kind-specific release has not happened` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the claim`'s `its kind`
            WHEN `a general protections application to the FWC (s 727)` THEN
                    (NOT `the claim`'s `the FWC issued its certificate`)
                OR  `the claim`'s `the parties then agreed to FWC arbitration`
            WHEN `an unlawful termination application to the FWC (s 730)` THEN
                    (NOT `the claim`'s `the FWC issued its certificate`)
                OR  `the claim`'s `the parties then agreed to FWC arbitration`
            WHEN `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)` THEN
                    NOT `the claim`'s `it failed because the FWC found a genuine redundancy`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 725: the new claim is barred if an earlier claim of ANOTHER kind still counts. A second claim of the same kind is
-- not barred by s 725 (READING: s 725 speaks of "any other of those sections"; whether a second application of the same
-- kind may be made is left to the forum).
@export May I now make this dismissal claim, given the claims I have already made (s 725)?
GIVEN `the new claim` IS A `Dismissal claim` @desc The kind of claim or complaint about the dismissal you want to make now
      `my earlier claims` IS A LIST OF `Earlier claim` @desc The claims or complaints about the dismissal you have already made
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make this dismissal claim` IF
    NOT (any (GIVEN c YIELD (`Does this earlier claim still count` c) AND (NOT (c's `its kind` EQUALS `the new claim`))) `my earlier claims`)

-- s 723: "A person must not make an unlawful termination application in relation to conduct if the person is entitled
-- to make a general protections court application in relation to the conduct."
@export May I make an unlawful termination application instead (s 723)?
GIVEN `I am entitled to make a general protections court application about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to make a general protections court application about the same conduct (a national system employee usually is)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make an unlawful termination application` IF
    NOT `I am entitled to make a general protections court application about it`

-- Which of the seven kinds are still open to me under s 725 alone (time limits, eligibility and s 723 are separate
-- questions).
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Dismissal claim`
      `my earlier claims` IS A LIST OF `Earlier claim`
      GIVETH A LIST OF `Dismissal claim`
`the kind if open` MEANS
    IF `May I make this dismissal claim` `the kind` `my earlier claims` THEN LIST `the kind` ELSE EMPTY

@export Which kinds of dismissal claim does s 725 still leave open to me?
GIVEN `my earlier claims` IS A LIST OF `Earlier claim` @desc The claims or complaints about the dismissal you have already made
GIVETH A LIST OF `Dismissal claim`
DECIDE `Which dismissal claims are still open to me` IS
    concat OF LIST
        `the kind if open` `a bargaining order application (s 726)` `my earlier claims`,
        `the kind if open` `a general protections application to the FWC (s 727)` `my earlier claims`,
        `the kind if open` `a general protections court application (s 728)` `my earlier claims`,
        `the kind if open` `an unfair dismissal application (s 729)` `my earlier claims`,
        `the kind if open` `an unlawful termination application to the FWC (s 730)` `my earlier claims`,
        `the kind if open` `an unlawful termination court application (s 731)` `my earlier claims`,
        `the kind if open` `a complaint under another law (s 732)` `my earlier claims`
